{"id":"u-fb63ebea-73d2-4b10-ad76-543f60ba3775","src":"community","title":"Spine-Safe Full Body Hypertrophy (5-Day Machine Fo","author":"Ziad Khaled","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/iiFVrP-spine-safe-full-body-hypertrophy-5-day-machine-fo","desc":"This is a 5-day full body hypertrophy program designed to help you build muscle, regain strength, and train consistently without putting unnecessary stress on your lower back.\n\nMost programs focus only on lifting heavier. That often leads to poor movement, imbalance, and injury. This program is built differently. It combines effective hypertrophy training with controlled movement, balanced volume, and a clear progression system so you can grow safely and consistently.\n\nThe structure is machine-focused to reduce instability and protect your spine. At the same time, it includes core work, glute training, and posterior chain development to actively support your lower back.\n\nHow the 8 weeks work\n\nWeek 1\nLearn the movements and focus on control. Keep effort moderate.\n\nWeek 2\nImprove stability and confidence. Clean up technique.\n\nWeek 3\nStart increasing weight or reps when you reach the top of the rep range.\n\nWeek 4\nHandle more volume at the same quality. Build consistency.\n\nWeek 5\nStrength improves. Push closer to your limits with control.\n\nWeek 6\nHigh output phase. Strong performance across all exercises.\n\nWeek 7\nPeak intensity. Hardest week but still controlled.\n\nWeek 8\nDeload. Reduce volume by about 40 percent and allow recovery.\n\nProgressive overload\nEach exercise has a rep range. When you reach the top of that range for all sets, increase the weight in your next session.\nIf you cannot reach the top, stay at the same weight and improve reps or control.\n\nRPE guidelines\n\nWeeks 1 to 2\nRPE 7 to 8\n\nWeeks 3 to 6\nRPE 8 to 8.5\n\nWeek 7\nRPE 8.5 to 9\n\nWeek 8\nRPE 6 to 7\n\nCore and lower back work always stays at RPE 6 to 7.\n\nWho this is for\n- People returning to training\n- Anyone managing lower back sensitivity\n- Lifters who want structure and consistency\n- Anyone who wants to build muscle without unnecessary risk\n\nTrain with control. Progress with purpose. Stay consistent.","level":["Intermediate","Novice"],"goals":["Athletics","Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":60,"joins":5,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-10-13T18:27:58.570Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Day 1","Day 2","Day 3","Day 4","Day 5"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Chest Press (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":8,"x":4}]},{"n":"Incline Chest Press (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Chest Fly (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Shoulder Press (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Tricep Rope Push Down (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Pallof Press","sets":[{"r":12,"rpe":6,"rpeHi":7,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Leg Press","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":8,"x":4}]},{"n":"Hack Squat","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":8,"x":4}]},{"n":"Leg Extension","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":8,"x":4}]},{"n":"Seated Hamstring Curl","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Hip Thrust (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":8,"x":4}]},{"n":"Hip Abductor (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Hip Adductor (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Seated Calf Raise","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":8,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Chest Supported Row (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":8,"x":4}]},{"n":"Lat Pulldown","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":8,"x":4}]},{"n":"Pull-Up (Assisted)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Rear Delt Fly (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":8,"x":